---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Scale and the Errand — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 61"
  description="Bekhorot 61: weigh the evidence for what Rabbi Yehuda does with the eleventh animal, then send an agent to separate tithe and teruma and see which mistakes bind the owner."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@300;400;700;900&display=swap" />

  <style is:global>
    :root { --night:#14121a; --card:#1e1b27; --line:#3a3548; --ink:#efe8dc; --mist:#a9a2b8; --gold:#e6b65a; --grass:#8fc27a; --red:#e3735e; --sky:#8fb4e8; }
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    .he { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; direction: rtl; }
    .t-ink { color: var(--ink) !important; }
    .t-mist { color: var(--mist) !important; }
    .t-gold { color: var(--gold) !important; }
    .t-grass { color: var(--grass) !important; }
    .t-red { color: var(--red) !important; }
    a.ref { color: var(--gold) !important; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    .stn { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 2.25rem 0; }
    .card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: .6rem; padding: 1rem; }
    .btn { border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: .4rem; padding: .5rem .8rem; font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.4; text-align: start; background: transparent; color: var(--ink) !important; cursor: pointer; }
    .btn:hover:not(:disabled) { background: var(--card); }
    .btn:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: .5; }
    .btn.on { border-color: var(--gold); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--gold); background: var(--card); opacity: 1; }
    .btn.ok { background: #1f331e; border-color: var(--grass); opacity: 1; }
    .btn.no { background: #3d1e19; border-color: var(--red); opacity: 1; }
    button:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .note { border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--line); padding: .3rem .8rem; font-size: .93rem; line-height: 1.65; margin-top: .75rem; color: var(--ink) !important; }
    .note.ok { border-color: var(--grass); } .note.no { border-color: var(--red); } .note.tk { border-color: var(--gold); }
    .row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; align-items: center; }
    .beam-wrap { position: relative; height: 9.5rem; margin: .5rem 0 1rem; }
    .beam { position: absolute; left: 8%; right: 8%; top: 2.2rem; height: .45rem; background: var(--gold); border-radius: 1rem; transform-origin: 50% 50%; transition: transform .8s cubic-bezier(.3,1.4,.5,1); }
    .post { position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 2.5rem; width: .5rem; height: 6rem; margin-left: -.25rem; background: var(--line); border-radius: .3rem; }
    .pan { position: absolute; top: 4.3rem; width: 40%; min-height: 3.3rem; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 0 0 .8rem .8rem; padding: .3rem; font-size: .8rem; transition: transform .8s cubic-bezier(.3,1.4,.5,1); }
    .pan h4 { font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mist) !important; }
    .pan.l { left: 1%; } .pan.r { right: 1%; }
    .chip { display: inline-block; background: #2b2740; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 1rem; padding: .05rem .5rem; margin: .1rem; font-size: .75rem; color: var(--ink) !important; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .beam, .pan { transition: none; } }
  </style>

  <main class="frank max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8" style="background:var(--night)">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="ref" href="/daf/">← Daf Yomi games</a></p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-black !text-amber-300 mt-2">⚖️ The Scale and the Errand</h1>
    <p class="he text-xl t-mist mt-1">בכורות ס״א</p>
    <p class="t-ink mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      A shepherd calls the wrong animal "tenth." The eleventh has now been called holy by mistake. What happens to it?
      Today's daf (<a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.61a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bekhorot 61a</a>)
      first weighs the evidence for what Rabbi Yehuda says, then asks when an <i>agent's</i> mistake binds the owner.
      Two rounds: a scale, and an errand.
    </p>

    <section class="stn" id="scale">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold !text-amber-300">Round 1 · The Scale of Rabbi Yehuda</h2>
      <p class="t-ink mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        The Gemara opens with a baraita that says both animals "must die" and assigns it to Rabbi Yehuda, who treats a mis-designated tithe as a
        <i>temura</i> (substitute) that is left to die (<a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.61a.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">61a:2</a>).
        Then it challenges that. For each source, say which pan it drops onto: does Rabbi Yehuda's <b>eleventh animal</b> get <b>sacrificed</b> or <b>die</b>?
      </p>
      <div class="card mt-4">
        <div class="beam-wrap" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="post"></div>
          <div class="beam" id="beam"></div>
          <div class="pan l" id="panL"><h4>Sacrificed</h4><div id="chipsL"></div></div>
          <div class="pan r" id="panR"><h4>Dies</h4><div id="chipsR"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div id="evidence"></div>
      </div>
      <div id="twist" class="mt-4"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="stn" id="errand">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold !text-amber-300">Round 2 · The Agent's Errand</h2>
      <p class="t-ink mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        An owner says: "Go separate animal tithe for me." The agent errs. Choose the mistake and whose view you follow, and see whether it stands
        (<a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.61a.10" target="_blank" rel="noopener">61a:10</a>).
        Then try the same errand with <b>teruma</b>, where the mishna says a different outcome (<a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.61a.11-13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">61a:11–13</a>).
      </p>
      <div class="card mt-4">
        <p class="t-mist text-sm uppercase tracking-wide">1 · Whose ruling?</p>
        <div class="row mt-1" id="sage"></div>
        <p class="t-mist text-sm uppercase tracking-wide mt-4">2 · What did the agent do?</p>
        <div class="row mt-1" id="acts"></div>
        <div id="verdict" class="mt-3" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card mt-6">
        <p class="t-mist text-sm uppercase tracking-wide">The teruma dial</p>
        <p class="t-ink text-sm mt-1">The owner's wishes are unknown, so the agent should take the middle measure. Slide the dial to what he actually separated.</p>
        <label for="dial" class="t-ink block mt-3">Separated: <b id="dialOut" class="t-gold">1/50 of the produce</b></label>
        <input id="dial" type="range" min="40" max="60" step="10" value="50" class="w-full mt-2" aria-describedby="dialNote" />
        <div class="row justify-between t-mist text-xs" style="justify-content:space-between"><span>1/40 (generous)</span><span>1/50 (middle)</span><span>1/60 (sparing)</span></div>
        <div id="dialNote" class="note tk" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <button class="btn mt-3" id="why">Why is teruma different from tithe?</button>
        <div id="whyOut"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="stn" id="learn">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold !text-amber-300">Learn the real daf</h2>
      <ul class="t-ink leading-relaxed list-disc ml-5 mt-2 space-y-1">
        <li><a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.61a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bekhorot 61a</a> and <a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.61b" target="_blank" rel="noopener">61b</a> on Sefaria</li>
        <li><a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.61a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rashi</a> (14 comments), <a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.61a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rabbeinu Gershom</a> (19), <a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.61a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Steinsaltz</a> (13) and <a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Ktav_Yad_Rashi_on_Bekhorot.61a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ktav Yad Rashi</a> (11)</li>
        <li>The mishna about the agent and teruma: <a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Terumot.4.4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Terumot 4:4</a></li>
        <li>The Sifra on the peace offering that includes the eleventh: <a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Leviticus.3.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lev. 3:1</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script is:inline>
    const R = (r, l) => `<a class="ref" href="https://www.sefaria.org/${r}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${l}</a>`;
    const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

    /* ---------- Round 1 ---------- */
    const EV = [
      { id: 'meir', name: 'The mishna: "If it were a substitute it would not be sacrificed" (Rabbi Meir)', ans: 'L',
        why: `Rabbi Meir argues that the eleventh isn't a substitute because a substitute of tithe isn't sacrificed. By inference, Rabbi Yehuda holds the eleventh <b>is</b> sacrificed despite its status (${R('Bekhorot.61a.3','61a:3')}).` },
      { id: 'bar', name: 'The baraita: the difference from a peace offering is only that the eleventh "does not render its substitute sanctified"', ans: 'L',
        why: `Stated as Rabbi Yehuda's view. If that's the <i>only</i> difference, the eleventh itself is sacrificed like a peace offering (${R('Bekhorot.61a.4','61a:4')}).` },
      { id: 'sifra', name: 'The Sifra on "If his offering be a sacrifice of peace offerings" (Lev. 3:1)', ans: 'L',
        why: `Its anonymous author is Rabbi Yehuda, and the verse includes the eleventh as a peace offering. The ninth is not included, since a substitute sanctifies only after the original is sanctified (${R('Bekhorot.61a.5-7','61a:5–7')}).` },
      { id: 'both', name: 'The opening baraita: two animals both called tenth "must die"', ans: 'R',
        why: `This one points to death and was first assigned to Rabbi Yehuda (${R('Bekhorot.61a.2','61a:2')}). But the three sources above say he sacrifices the eleventh.` },
    ];
    const placed = {};
    function renderEv() {
      $('evidence').innerHTML = EV.map((e) => {
        const p = placed[e.id];
        const cls = (side) => 'btn' + (p ? (side === e.ans ? ' ok' : (p === side ? ' no' : '')) : '');
        return `<div class="mb-4"><p class="t-ink">${e.name}</p>
          <div class="row mt-1"><button class="${cls('L')}" data-e="${e.id}" data-s="L" ${p ? 'disabled' : ''}>Sacrificed</button>
          <button class="${cls('R')}" data-e="${e.id}" data-s="R" ${p ? 'disabled' : ''}>Dies</button></div>
          ${p ? `<div class="note ${p === e.ans ? 'ok' : 'no'}">${p === e.ans ? 'Yes. ' : 'Not quite. '}${e.why}</div>` : ''}</div>`;
      }).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('#evidence button').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        placed[b.dataset.e] = b.dataset.s; renderEv(); tilt();
      }));
    }
    function tilt() {
      const side = (s) => EV.filter((e) => e.ans === s && placed[e.id]).map((e) => `<span class="chip">${e.id}</span>`).join('');
      // chips show where each source *actually* belongs, once placed
      $('chipsL').innerHTML = side('L'); $('chipsR').innerHTML = side('R');
      const l = EV.filter((e) => e.ans === 'L' && placed[e.id]).length, r = EV.filter((e) => e.ans === 'R' && placed[e.id]).length;
      $('beam').style.transform = `rotate(${(l - r) * -3}deg)`;
      $('panL').style.transform = `translateY(${(l - r) * 4}px)`;
      $('panR').style.transform = `translateY(${(r - l) * 4}px)`;
      if (Object.keys(placed).length === EV.length) twist();
    }
    function twist() {
      $('twist').innerHTML = `<div class="card"><p class="t-ink">The scale says Rabbi Yehuda <b>sacrifices</b> the eleventh. So whose is the baraita where two animals called "tenth" both die? Rabbi Shimon son of Rabbi Abba tells Rabbi Yoḥanan (${R('Bekhorot.61a.8','61a:8')}). Pick his answer:</p>
        <div class="row mt-2" id="twOpts"></div><div id="twOut"></div></div>`;
      const opts = [
        ['a', 'It is Rabbi Meir\'s, who treats the eleventh as a substitute.', false, 'No. Rabbi Meir\'s statement was used to prove Rabbi Yehuda\'s view, and nothing in the daf makes him the author here.'],
        ['b', 'It speaks of tithe nowadays, with no Temple: the animals die lest the owner shear, work or eat them before a blemish.', true, `Right. The Gemara adds that it names two animals only because of a "not necessary" style: with one it is obvious, but with two the loss is great and he might wait for a blemish and eat them (${R('Bekhorot.61a.9','61a:9')}).`],
        ['c', 'Rabbi Yehuda changed his mind.', false, 'No. The Gemara resolves it by changing the case, not the sage.'],
      ];
      $('twOpts').innerHTML = opts.map((o) => `<button class="btn" data-o="${o[0]}">${o[1]}</button>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('#twOpts button').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const o = opts.find((x) => x[0] === b.dataset.o);
        document.querySelectorAll('#twOpts button').forEach((x) => { x.disabled = true; });
        b.classList.add(o[2] ? 'ok' : 'no');
        $('twOut').innerHTML = `<div class="note ${o[2] ? 'ok' : 'no'}">${o[3]}</div>`;
      }));
    }
    renderEv();

    /* ---------- Round 2 ---------- */
    let sage = 'pappi';
    const SAGES = { pappi: 'Rav Pappi (in Rava\'s name)', pappa: 'Rav Pappa' };
    const ACTS = {
      ninth: { label: 'Called the ninth animal "tenth"', out: {
        pappi: ['tk', 'It is <b>sanctified</b>: it cannot be eaten until it has a blemish. The owner doesn\'t mind this error much, since the animal isn\'t lost entirely.'],
        pappa: ['no', 'It is <b>not sanctified</b>. The owner can say: "I sent you for my benefit, not my detriment." An agent\'s authority doesn\'t cover acting against the owner.'] } },
      eleventh: { label: 'Called the eleventh animal "tenth"', out: {
        pappi: ['no', 'It is <b>not sanctified</b> as a peace offering: an owner wouldn\'t tolerate losing the animal entirely.'],
        pappa: ['no', 'Rav Pappa says "even" the ninth is not sanctified when the agent errs, so the eleventh, a worse loss, is not sanctified either.'] } },
    };
    function renderSage() {
      $('sage').innerHTML = Object.entries(SAGES).map(([k, v]) => `<button class="btn ${k === sage ? 'on' : ''}" data-k="${k}">${v}</button>`).join('');
      document.querySelectorAll('#sage button').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => { sage = b.dataset.k; renderSage(); $('verdict').innerHTML = ''; }));
    }
    $('acts').innerHTML = Object.entries(ACTS).map(([k, v]) => `<button class="btn" data-a="${k}">${v.label}</button>`).join('');
    document.querySelectorAll('#acts button').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      document.querySelectorAll('#acts button').forEach((x) => x.classList.remove('on')); b.classList.add('on');
      const [c, t] = ACTS[b.dataset.a].out[sage];
      $('verdict').innerHTML = `<div class="note ${c}">${t} (${R('Bekhorot.61a.10', '61a:10')})</div>`;
    }));
    renderSage();

    const DIAL = { 40: 'Valid teruma. The mishna says subtracting ten from the denominator (1/40) is still teruma; a generous person gives this much.',
      50: 'The intermediate measure, what the agent should take when he doesn\'t know the owner\'s wishes.',
      60: 'Valid teruma. Adding ten to the denominator (1/60) is still teruma; a stingy person gives this much.' };
    function dial() {
      const v = $('dial').value; $('dialOut').textContent = `1/${v} of the produce`; $('dialNote').textContent = DIAL[v];
    }
    $('dial').addEventListener('input', dial); dial();
    $('why').addEventListener('click', () => {
      $('why').disabled = true;
      $('whyOut').innerHTML = `<div class="note ok">Teruma has no fixed measure; some give generously and some sparingly, so the agent can say "I estimated you were one of these." But in tithe, calling the wrong animal is a <b>mistake</b>, and the owner can say "I did not want you to make a mistake" (${R('Bekhorot.61a.13','61a:13')}, the Sages' answer to the challenge of ${R('Bekhorot.61a.11-12','61a:11–12')}).</div>`;
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
